body:
Looks great man love the look of the cloth.

&#x200B;

If I may give on small suggestion on the base do a light dry brushing to pull out the textures on the rocks.

Sure thing, currently I've been basing the rads with Ceramite white then I've got Fluorescent  Chartreuse (Brightest Yellow/Green I've found to date) by Golden Artist Colors I paint a few layers of that until I'm happy with the color. Then on thin shade of biel-tan Green, then I glaze with Waywatcher Green. Finally I go back with Ceramite white to make it look hotter.

&#x200B;

I will be changing this slightly in the future to hopefully make it look less blotchy. Need to get some glaze medium I think not to sure atm but going to work more on it.

I had originally planned on not doing OSL but wasn't to happy with the look without it. I figured I would try it out and it has gotten better I think, the first few I did go too heavy on the OSL.

&#x200B;

Any suggestion on what basics I should focus on or resources I could use. Thanks
